<title>DENMARK: Danske Bank 1996 pre-tax profits down.</title>
<headline>Danske Bank 1996 pre-tax profits down.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>12 mths to December 31 1996</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Pre-tax result &amp; extraordinary items   5,396 vs  6,034</p>
<p> Group net result			     3,653 vs  3,631</p>
<p> Losses and bad debt provisions	     637 vs  1,254</p>
<p> Securities and forex results	     1,734 vs  2,297</p>
<p> Net interest and fees income	     9,395 vs  9,593</p>
<p> Result of financial items		 11,319 vs 12,072</p>
<p> Group pre-tax result			4,642  vs  5,088</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (percent)		  16  vs  16</p>
<p>Balance end-1996 451.8 billion vs 390.0 billion end-1995</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Danish banking group is Den Danske Bank A/S, Denmark's biggest bank. It said in a statement that it expected little growth in core earnings in 1997 and no fall in costs. The pre-tax and extraordinary items result was above average analyst expectations of 4.800 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969652</p>
</text>
